1
00:00:00,275 --> 00:00:02,285
大家好，我是马特·沃克。
Hi everybody, I'm Matt Walker.

2
00:00:02,285 --> 00:00:04,345
我教授哲学与人文学科，
I teach philosophy and humanities

3
00:00:04,345 --> 00:00:06,740
任教于新加坡的耶鲁—新加坡国立大学学院。
at Yale-NUS College in Singapore.

4
00:00:06,825 --> 00:00:08,455
今天我将探讨，
Today I'm going to take a look at

5
00:00:08,455 --> 00:00:10,490
孟子关于人性的观点。
Mengzi's views on human nature.

6
00:00:10,575 --> 00:00:12,665
具体来说，我将考察，
In particular, I'm going to take a look at

7
00:00:12,665 --> 00:00:16,160
孟子如何为“人性本善”的主张辩护。
Mengzi's defense of the claim that human nature is good.

8
00:00:16,865 --> 00:00:18,970
孟子，在西方也被称为Mencius，
Mengzi, also known as Mencius,

9
00:00:19,065 --> 00:00:21,200
是一位早期儒家哲学家。
was an early Confucian philosopher.

10
00:00:21,395 --> 00:00:23,860
他生活在公元前四世纪。
He lived in the 300s BCE.

11
00:00:24,025 --> 00:00:26,645
与孔子一样，孟子致力于捍卫，
Like Confucius, Mengzi was concerned to defend

12
00:00:26,645 --> 00:00:29,780
一种关于人类美好生活的特定观念。
a certain conception of the good life for human beings.

13
00:00:30,085 --> 00:00:31,955
我们可以将这种美好生活的观念，
Call this conception of the good life

14
00:00:31,955 --> 00:00:35,150
称为儒家之“道”。
the Confucian Way or the Confucian Tao.

15
00:00:35,415 --> 00:00:36,845
按照儒家之道，
According to the Confucian Way,

16
00:00:36,845 --> 00:00:39,995
拥有仁、义，
possessing virtues like benevolence, righteousness,

17
00:00:39,995 --> 00:00:41,750
以及礼、智等美德，
propriety, and wisdom

18
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:43,790
是过好人生的核心所在。
are central to a life well lived.

19
00:00:44,305 --> 00:00:46,940
当孟子说“人性本善”时，
When Mengzi says that human nature is good,

20
00:00:47,085 --> 00:00:48,905
他的意思是，人类
Mengzi's thought is that human beings

21
00:00:48,905 --> 00:00:52,650
天生就具有趋向这些美德的潜能或倾向。
have innate potentials or predispositions towards such virtues.

22
00:00:52,765 --> 00:00:55,560
我们自然地倾向于这些美德。
We naturally tend toward these virtues.

23
00:00:55,865 --> 00:00:56,870
正如孟子所说：
As Mengzi says,

24
00:00:57,045 --> 00:01:00,670
“仁、义、礼、智，
"Benevolence, righteousness, propriety, and wisdom

25
00:01:00,765 --> 00:01:03,190
并非由外界强加于我。
are not welded to us externally.

26
00:01:03,505 --> 00:01:05,070
而是我们本来就具有的。”
We inherently have them."

27
00:01:05,955 --> 00:01:07,210
在阐述这一观点时，
In presenting this view,

28
00:01:07,295 --> 00:01:09,740
孟子使用了一个农业方面的比喻。
Mengzi uses an agricultural metaphor.

29
00:01:09,895 --> 00:01:12,515
他将这些潜能和倾向，
He describes these potentials and predispositions

30
00:01:12,515 --> 00:01:14,720
描述为美德的萌芽，也就是“善端”。
as sprouts of virtue.

31
00:01:15,025 --> 00:01:17,735
孟子进一步指出，这些善端，
Mengzi in turn locates these sprouts of virtue

32
00:01:17,735 --> 00:01:19,665
存在于人的“心”之中，
in the heart, or heart-mind,

33
00:01:19,665 --> 00:01:22,215
在孟子看来，心是，
which Mengzi identifies as the seat

34
00:01:22,215 --> 00:01:25,230
我们的认知与情感倾向的所在。
of our cognitive and affective dispositions.

35
00:01:25,905 --> 00:01:29,565
孟子认为，如果我们充分培育这些善端，
Mengzi's thought is that if we fully cultivate our sprouts,

36
00:01:29,565 --> 00:01:32,325
悉心培养我们趋向美德的倾向，
if we tend to our predispositions toward virtue

37
00:01:32,325 --> 00:01:33,955
并成为具备完善德性的人，
and become fully virtuous,

38
00:01:33,955 --> 00:01:36,890
我们的人性就能得到充分实现。
then we will bring our human nature to full fruition.

39
00:01:37,035 --> 00:01:39,400
我们也就能作为人而蓬勃发展。
We will flourish as human beings.

40
00:01:39,715 --> 00:01:41,535
但孟子提出了什么证据，
But what evidence does Mengzi adduce

41
00:01:41,535 --> 00:01:43,590
来支持“人性本善”的观点呢？
for the view that human nature is good?

42
00:01:43,715 --> 00:01:45,095
换句话说，他依据什么，
On what basis, in other words,

43
00:01:45,095 --> 00:01:47,715
认为我们具有这样的倾向，
does Mengzi think that we have such predispositions

44
00:01:47,715 --> 00:01:50,260
会趋向仁、义等美德呢？
toward benevolence, righteousness, and the like?

45
00:01:50,925 --> 00:01:52,175
这里，我想考察，
Here, I want to take a look at

46
00:01:52,175 --> 00:01:54,335
《孟子》中最著名的论证之一。
one of the most famous arguments in the Mengzi.

47
00:01:54,335 --> 00:01:56,940
它见于《孟子·公孙丑上》第六章。
It appears in Mengzi 2A6.

48
00:01:57,105 --> 00:01:59,940
和哲学史上的其他一些著名论证一样，
Like some other famous arguments in the history of philosophy,

49
00:02:00,165 --> 00:02:02,060
这一论证涉及一个思想实验。
it involves a thought experiment.

50
00:02:02,215 --> 00:02:04,375
我将孟子的这个思想实验，
I'll call Mengzi's thought experiment

51
00:02:04,375 --> 00:02:06,580
称为“孺子将入井”的案例。
"The Child and the Well Case."

52
00:02:06,945 --> 00:02:09,220
各位，请认识一下小瑞娅。
Ladies and gentlemen, meet Little Rhea.

53
00:02:09,575 --> 00:02:12,065
假设小瑞娅正摇摇晃晃地，
Suppose that Little Rhea is toddling right along

54
00:02:12,065 --> 00:02:13,270
穿过这片田野。
through this field.

55
00:02:13,795 --> 00:02:16,610
再假设，她浑然不觉地，
And suppose further that she's heading obliviously

56
00:02:16,655 --> 00:02:19,280
径直朝这口看上去很吓人的井走去。
right toward this scary-looking well.

57
00:02:19,455 --> 00:02:20,750
井就在那儿。
There's the well.

58
00:02:20,895 --> 00:02:23,000
小瑞娅正蹒跚着往前走。
There's Little Rhea toddling along.

59
00:02:23,135 --> 00:02:25,200
越来越近了。啊！
Getting closer. Ah!

60
00:02:25,415 --> 00:02:26,445
呼，我想我应该补充一句：
Phew, I guess I should add

61
00:02:26,445 --> 00:02:28,760
你刚才看到的只是情景演示。
that what you saw was only a dramatization.

62
00:02:28,835 --> 00:02:31,455
孟子认为，任何人只要看到小瑞娅，
According to Mengzi, anyone who saw Little Rhea

63
00:02:31,455 --> 00:02:33,125
就要蹒跚着掉进那口井里，
about to toddle into that well

64
00:02:33,125 --> 00:02:36,650
都会产生一种即时、不假思索的本能反应。
would have an immediate, non-reflective gut reaction.

65
00:02:36,985 --> 00:02:39,170
正如《孟子·公孙丑上》第六章所说，
As Mengzi says in 2A6,

66
00:02:39,385 --> 00:02:42,900
人人都会顿生“怵惕恻隐之心”。
anyone would feel a surge of alarm and compassion.

67
00:02:43,145 --> 00:02:46,055
事实上，只要把这个孩子与井的案例，
Indeed, simply imagining the child in the well case

68
00:02:46,055 --> 00:02:47,480
生动地想象出来，
vividly to yourselves,

69
00:02:47,635 --> 00:02:49,510
你或许就能感受到几分这种惊惧。
you might feel something of this alarm.

70
00:02:50,005 --> 00:02:51,725
那么，从孟子的这个思想实验，
Okay, so what should we conclude

71
00:02:51,725 --> 00:02:54,940
也就是“孺子将入井”的案例中，我们该得出什么结论呢？
from Mengzi's child and the well thought experiment?

72
00:02:54,995 --> 00:02:58,115
孟子认为，我们不假思索的本能反应，
According to Mengzi, our non-reflective gut reaction

73
00:02:58,115 --> 00:03:00,120
面对小瑞娅即将遭遇的危险时的反应，
to Little Rhea's looming danger

74
00:03:00,125 --> 00:03:03,330
表明我们天生就具有趋向仁的倾向。
shows that we have innate predispositions toward benevolence.

75
00:03:03,415 --> 00:03:04,460
在孟子看来，
On Mengzi's view,

76
00:03:04,555 --> 00:03:08,200
我们对小瑞娅可能遭遇不幸的反应，是与生俱来的。
our response to Little Rhea's potential disaster is hardwired.

77
00:03:08,425 --> 00:03:11,545
人类天生就具有这样的倾向：
Human beings, by nature, are simply predisposed

78
00:03:11,545 --> 00:03:13,685
会感到惊惧与同情，
to respond with alarm and compassion

79
00:03:13,685 --> 00:03:17,020
当他们看到无力自卫的无辜者即将受害时。
when they see defenseless innocents about to face harm.

80
00:03:17,025 --> 00:03:19,720
孟子强调，我们的惊惧与同情，
And our alarm and compassion Mengzi insists

81
00:03:19,875 --> 00:03:22,960
体现了人性中仁的萌芽，也就是“仁之端”。
reveals the sprout of benevolence in human nature.

82
00:03:23,355 --> 00:03:24,535
当然，这并不表明，
To be sure, it doesn't show

83
00:03:24,535 --> 00:03:27,485
我们已经拥有充分发展的仁德。
that we possess the fully developed virtue of benevolence,

84
00:03:27,485 --> 00:03:29,225
但孟子认为，它揭示了，
but Mengzi thinks that it reveals

85
00:03:29,225 --> 00:03:31,365
仁的胚芽或萌芽，
the germ or bud of benevolence,

86
00:03:31,365 --> 00:03:34,005
即仁的一种初始形态，
a kind of proto-version of benevolence

87
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:36,330
可以通过培育走向成熟。
that can be cultivated to maturity.

88
00:03:36,805 --> 00:03:38,260
然而，孟子也承认，
Mengzi recognizes, however,

89
00:03:38,295 --> 00:03:41,625
人们可能对我们的反应提出不同的解释。
that one might offer different accounts of our reactions.

90
00:03:41,625 --> 00:03:43,640
按照另一种解释，
According to one alternative proposal,

91
00:03:43,705 --> 00:03:45,955
也许一个人对小瑞娅遇险的反应，
perhaps one's response to Little Rhea's danger

92
00:03:45,955 --> 00:03:47,930
其实出于工具性的动机。
is instrumentally motivated.

93
00:03:48,035 --> 00:03:48,850
换句话说，
In other words,

94
00:03:48,965 --> 00:03:52,090
一个人之所以对小瑞娅感到惊惧与同情，
maybe one feels alarm and compassion for Little Rhea

95
00:03:52,175 --> 00:03:54,470
也许是因为他心中有某些目的，
because one has certain ends in view

96
00:03:54,575 --> 00:03:56,930
或者因为他另有所图。
or because one has ulterior motives.

97
00:03:57,415 --> 00:04:00,390
然而，孟子拒绝了这种工具性的解释。
Mengzi, however, rejects this instrumental account.

98
00:04:00,745 --> 00:04:03,090
孟子说，听到小瑞娅的遭遇时，
Hearing about Little Rhea, Mengzi says,

99
00:04:03,235 --> 00:04:04,960
一个人会感到惊惧与同情，
one would feel alarm and compassion

100
00:04:05,165 --> 00:04:08,730
并不是因为他想讨好孩子的父母，
not because one sought to get in good with the child's parents.

101
00:04:08,735 --> 00:04:12,750
也不是因为他想在乡邻朋友中博取美名，
not because one wanted fame among their neighbors and friends,

102
00:04:13,115 --> 00:04:17,550
更不是因为他厌恶孩子的哭声。
and not because one would dislike the sound of the child's cries.

103
00:04:17,995 --> 00:04:19,575
孟子认为，关键在于，
What's important, Mengzi thinks,

104
00:04:19,575 --> 00:04:21,985
我们这种惊惧与同情的反应，
is that our alarmed and compassionate response

105
00:04:21,985 --> 00:04:24,100
是自发而不假思索的。
is spontaneous and unthinking.

106
00:04:24,595 --> 00:04:27,790
这表明，我们的反应并不经过权衡算计。
That shows that our response emerges without calculation.

107
00:04:28,325 --> 00:04:31,720
不过，孟子的人性观还面临另一个挑战。
Still, Mengzi's view of human nature faces another challenge.

108
00:04:31,895 --> 00:04:35,135
“人性本善”似乎显然是错误的。
It seems demonstrably false that human nature is good.

109
00:04:35,135 --> 00:04:38,410
如果人性本善，恶德就应当很少见。
If human nature is good, then vice should be rare.

110
00:04:38,495 --> 00:04:42,415
我们不该经常看到野蛮、劫掠、贪腐，
We shouldn't often see brutishness, plunder, venality,

111
00:04:42,415 --> 00:04:45,515
自私、恃权专横，以及其他恶劣品质。
selfishness, petty tyranny, and other nasty traits.

112
00:04:45,515 --> 00:04:47,190
但恶德却并不少见。
But vice isn't rare.

113
00:04:47,365 --> 00:04:49,750
因此，孟子的观点似乎是错误的。
Hence it might seem Mengzi's view is wrong.

114
00:04:49,985 --> 00:04:53,470
与孟子相反，人性看起来也许本就是恶的。
Contrary to Mengzi, it might seem human nature is bad.

115
00:04:54,125 --> 00:04:56,060
面对这类挑战时，
When faced with this kind of challenge,

116
00:04:56,145 --> 00:04:59,170
孟子的策略是让人性免于被归罪。
Mengzi's strategy is to get human nature off the hook.

117
00:04:59,335 --> 00:05:01,940
孟子主张，如果人变坏了，
If human beings are bad, Mengzi argues,

118
00:05:01,955 --> 00:05:04,040
那并不是因为他们的本性是恶的。
It's not because their nature is bad.

119
00:05:04,505 --> 00:05:06,380
孟子是这样阐述这一点的：
Mengzi puts the point this way.

120
00:05:06,535 --> 00:05:09,225
就人的本质而言，人能够为善。
As for their essence, human beings can become good.

121
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:12,050
这就是我所谓的人性本善。
This is what I mean by calling their natures good.

122
00:05:12,235 --> 00:05:13,865
至于他们变得不善，
As for their becoming not good,

123
00:05:13,865 --> 00:05:16,270
那并不是其天赋潜能的过错。
this is not the fault of their potential.

124
00:05:16,805 --> 00:05:18,910
或者，正如孟子在另一处所说，
Or, as Mengzi puts the point elsewhere,

125
00:05:19,135 --> 00:05:22,645
并非只有贤者才具有这种心，
it is not the case that only the worthy person has this heart,

126
00:05:22,645 --> 00:05:25,170
也就是勇气之心，或勇气的萌芽。
that is, the heart or sprout of courage.

127
00:05:25,345 --> 00:05:26,885
所有人都具有它。
All human beings have it.

128
00:05:26,885 --> 00:05:29,200
贤者只不过是从不丧失它而已。
The worthy person simply never loses it.

129
00:05:29,925 --> 00:05:32,465
换句话说，孟子完全明白，
In other words, Mengzi is fully aware

130
00:05:32,465 --> 00:05:34,840
世上到处都有坏人。
that the world is full of bad human beings.

131
00:05:35,085 --> 00:05:39,240
但孟子认为，不要把这种恶归咎于人性。
But Mengzi suggests don't blame human nature for such badness.

132
00:05:39,305 --> 00:05:42,890
相反，应该归因于人性的发展受到阻碍。
Instead, blame the stunting of human nature for such badness.

133
00:05:43,185 --> 00:05:46,000
人性确实具有趋向美德的倾向，
Human nature does have predispositions toward virtue,

134
00:05:46,135 --> 00:05:49,414
但这些倾向可能受到败坏。
but these predispositions can be corrupted.

